// =====================================================================
// SmartAttendance.ino  —  Single-file Arduino IDE version
//
// Tap an RFID card -> looked up against the roster -> saved to flash and
// queued in the outbox -> shown on the OLED + LEDs / buzzer -> a
// background FreeRTOS task uploads the outbox to a Google Sheet (HTTPS).
//
// A tap is NEVER lost: it is durable the moment it is accepted, and it
// stays queued until the backend confirms it.  Wi-Fi drops, backend
// outages, and power cuts are all handled.
//
// Duplicate attendance on the SAME calendar date is blocked both locally
// (Student.logged flag + NTP day-rollover) and by the Apps Script itself
// ("Duplicate" response = already in the sheet for today).
//
// ── Credentials (already filled in) ────────────────────────────────
//   Wi-Fi SSID     : Dark_98
//   Script URL     : https://script.google.com/macros/s/
//                    AKfycbztuadEKdYnplTQnfGBNoqNhyFn6njOKJKXBlCvy
//                    WCpuNw-58kDp0R0IYUAgswAPrGshA/exec
//   API key        : aae0deba654d5d36a9b143d6029e480a
//
// ── Libraries needed (install via Sketch → Include Library → Manage Libraries)
//   • MFRC522        (by GithubCommunity)
//   • Adafruit SSD1306
//   • Adafruit GFX Library
//   Board: "ESP32 Dev Module"  |  Upload speed: 921600  |  Port: your COM
// =====================================================================

